module iam

# ========================================
# IDENTITY PROVIDER TYPE (Organization-scoped)
# ========================================
# External platform trust relationships for federated authentication.
# Scoped to organization - each identity provider is owned by an org.
#
# Access model: RESTRICTED, managed by the organization's current admins
# Identity providers are administrative infrastructure, not discoverable
# content: they carry an organization's trust configuration. Plain members
# and viewer-role members of the organization see nothing. `owner` is
# computed, never stored: it is the organization's admins, as a team is
# managed, so a provider stays manageable whoever created it, and a creator
# who is demoted below admin or removed loses control of it with the role.
# Editing a provider decides who may sign in to the organization, so that
# control must end when the role that granted it does. The creator is
# recorded in the audit trail (kind_meta `owner_type` NONE).
#
# Permission pattern:
# - Org Admin (and org owner, through admin): full management
# - Direct viewer grant: can see the provider and who has access to it
# - Org Members and Viewers: no access (administrative resource)
#
# FGA tuple on creation (the kind's creation event: organization scope, no
# owner; private, so no visibility tuple):
# - identity_provider:idp_abc#organization@organization:planton
#
# Checks the handlers make: `can_create_idp` on the organization to
# create; `can_view` to get, get by reference, and to keep a row in the
# organization's list; `can_edit` to update and to link a managed
# organization; `can_delete` to delete.
#
# Platform tenancy (managed orgs):
# Each platform_managed organization is linked back to the identity
# provider that operates it. This makes the identity provider the FGA hub
# for the platform's tenant family, enabling visibility_platform: a
# blueprint in the platform's own org grants platform_viewer to
# identity_provider:<idp>#platform_user, which fans out to the members of
# every managed org — including orgs created later, with no per-resource
# backfill.
#
# FGA tuple on platform_managed org creation:
# - identity_provider:idp_abc#managed_org@organization:acme

type identity_provider
  relations
    # ========================================
    # PARENT ORGANIZATION
    # ========================================
    define organization: [organization]
    
    # ========================================
    # MANAGED ORGANIZATIONS (Platform Tenancy)
    # ========================================
    # Organizations operated by this identity provider on behalf of the
    # external platform (OrganizationSpec.identity_provider_ref mirrors
    # this edge in the data model).
    # FGA tuple: identity_provider:<idp_id>#managed_org@organization:<org_id>
    define managed_org: [organization]
    
    # All members of all managed organizations. This is the userset that
    # visibility_platform blueprints grant platform_viewer to.
    define platform_user: member from managed_org
    
    # ========================================
    # OWNERSHIP
    # ========================================
    # Every current admin of the provider's organization, and nobody else.
    define owner: admin from organization
    
    # ========================================
    # VIEWER ACCESS
    # ========================================
    # Owners (admins included) and direct viewer grants. Organization
    # members and viewers are deliberately absent.
    define viewer: ([identity_account] and affiliated from organization) or owner
    
    # ========================================
    # PERMISSIONS
    # ========================================
    define can_view: viewer
    define can_edit: owner
    define can_delete: owner
    
    # ========================================
    # IAM POLICY MANAGEMENT
    # ========================================
    define can_grant_access: owner
    define can_view_access: viewer
